1
00:00:01,159 --> 00:00:03,020
Far beyond the overworld

2
00:00:03,020 --> 00:00:04,850
lies the Endless Sea.

3
00:00:05,440 --> 00:00:07,550
Warm islands, bright reefs,

4
00:00:07,799 --> 00:00:10,259
a drowned city, and a trench so deep

5
00:00:10,259 --> 00:00:11,620
that the sunlight never

6
00:00:11,620 --> 00:00:13,109
reaches its floor.

7
00:00:15,060 --> 00:00:17,960
This is Beach Craft three point oh,

8
00:00:17,960 --> 00:00:18,699
Tides of the Deep,

9
00:00:18,699 --> 00:00:22,420
for Minecraft twenty six point three.

10
00:00:22,420 --> 00:00:24,709
In this film we take our time.

11
00:00:24,920 --> 00:00:26,660
We visit every biome,

12
00:00:26,660 --> 00:00:28,780
every place and every creature,

13
00:00:28,780 --> 00:00:29,600
we look at the blocks

14
00:00:29,600 --> 00:00:31,889
and items and how they work,

15
00:00:32,160 --> 00:00:32,679
and at the end

16
00:00:32,679 --> 00:00:34,799
we follow the whole story,

17
00:00:34,799 --> 00:00:36,609
the way a player would.

18
00:00:39,635 --> 00:00:41,735
The journey starts in the overworld.

19
00:00:41,735 --> 00:00:44,135
On sandy beaches stand short,

20
00:00:44,135 --> 00:00:46,365
dark stumps of driftwood.

21
00:00:47,785 --> 00:00:50,645
Four driftwood logs around one ancient

22
00:00:50,645 --> 00:00:53,455
energy make four portal frames.

23
00:00:54,085 --> 00:00:54,825
The energy comes

24
00:00:54,825 --> 00:00:56,425
from ancient broken rings,

25
00:00:56,425 --> 00:00:58,665
which hide in shipwreck treasure

26
00:00:58,665 --> 00:01:00,275
and ocean ruins.

27
00:01:01,960 --> 00:01:04,419
The frame is built like a nether portal,

28
00:01:04,419 --> 00:01:07,189
and the energy staff lights it.

29
00:01:08,934 --> 00:01:10,774
Step through, and you arrive

30
00:01:10,774 --> 00:01:12,154
on a driftwood platform

31
00:01:12,154 --> 00:01:13,804
high above the waves,

32
00:01:14,014 --> 00:01:15,804
with a portal back home.

33
00:01:18,784 --> 00:01:20,224
The Endless Sea is

34
00:01:20,224 --> 00:01:22,724
an archipelago: open water,

35
00:01:22,724 --> 00:01:24,684
islands, reefs and deep trenches,

36
00:01:24,684 --> 00:01:27,214
spread over twelve biomes.

37
00:01:28,934 --> 00:01:31,814
The Endless Sea itself is deep blue,

38
00:01:31,814 --> 00:01:33,184
open water.

39
00:01:33,474 --> 00:01:35,434
Kelp and seagrass grow on the floor,

40
00:01:35,434 --> 00:01:37,474
and bubble vents send columns

41
00:01:37,474 --> 00:01:39,524
of air up to the surface.

42
00:01:41,259 --> 00:01:42,939
In the kelp forest,

43
00:01:42,939 --> 00:01:44,359
the kelp grows very tall,

44
00:01:44,359 --> 00:01:45,179
and patches

45
00:01:45,179 --> 00:01:47,929
of glow kelp light the green water.

46
00:01:48,219 --> 00:01:50,029
Barnacles cover the rocks.

47
00:01:51,809 --> 00:01:54,779
The coral shallows are warm and clear.

48
00:01:55,349 --> 00:01:57,169
Between the reefs sit sea anemones,

49
00:01:57,169 --> 00:01:58,729
giant clams,

50
00:01:58,729 --> 00:02:01,089
starfish and spiny sea urchins,

51
00:02:01,089 --> 00:02:02,849
and pebbles of sea glass lie

52
00:02:02,849 --> 00:02:03,959
in the sand.

53
00:02:05,634 --> 00:02:08,564
The glowing lagoon is rare and dim.

54
00:02:08,814 --> 00:02:10,174
Glowing anemones,

55
00:02:10,174 --> 00:02:12,114
tube worms and glow kelp fill it

56
00:02:12,114 --> 00:02:13,464
with soft light.

57
00:02:15,134 --> 00:02:17,114
The drowned shelf is a flat,

58
00:02:17,114 --> 00:02:20,734
murky floor covered in concrete rubble: the ground

59
00:02:20,734 --> 00:02:22,944
of a city that the sea swallowed.

60
00:02:24,859 --> 00:02:27,399
The abyssal trench is the deepest water

61
00:02:27,399 --> 00:02:31,059
of all. Down there it is almost black,

62
00:02:31,059 --> 00:02:32,179
and only tube worms

63
00:02:32,179 --> 00:02:35,029
and glowing anemones light the basalt.

64
00:02:36,684 --> 00:02:38,704
The wreck graveyard is foggy,

65
00:02:38,704 --> 00:02:41,414
grey water, full of sunken ships.

66
00:02:43,159 --> 00:02:44,439
In the frost floes,

67
00:02:44,439 --> 00:02:47,359
icebergs and ice floes drift on cold,

68
00:02:47,359 --> 00:02:48,929
clear water.

69
00:02:50,484 --> 00:02:52,944
The palm isles have sandy beaches

70
00:02:52,944 --> 00:02:56,054
with shell sand, palm trees,

71
00:02:56,324 --> 00:02:59,054
beach grass and tall sea oats.

72
00:02:59,584 --> 00:03:00,724
Hibiscus and bird

73
00:03:00,724 --> 00:03:03,674
of paradise flowers grow between them,

74
00:03:03,824 --> 00:03:06,224
and seashells and sea glass wash up

75
00:03:06,224 --> 00:03:07,294
on the shore.

76
00:03:09,059 --> 00:03:11,849
Jungle isles are warm and wet,

77
00:03:12,059 --> 00:03:14,029
with jungle trees, bamboo,

78
00:03:14,459 --> 00:03:15,299
tropical ferns

79
00:03:15,299 --> 00:03:17,109
and wild pineapple bushes.

80
00:03:18,984 --> 00:03:21,864
Mangrove isles are low and muddy,

81
00:03:21,864 --> 00:03:24,134
with tangled roots and lily pads.

82
00:03:25,959 --> 00:03:28,099
And the volcanic isles are dark

83
00:03:28,099 --> 00:03:30,319
and rough: black sand,

84
00:03:30,319 --> 00:03:33,409
volcanic ash, pumice and basalt columns.

85
00:03:35,434 --> 00:03:36,834
Some of these natural

86
00:03:36,834 --> 00:03:38,444
blocks do something.

87
00:03:38,814 --> 00:03:41,294
A giant clam opens and closes,

88
00:03:41,294 --> 00:03:43,644
and an open clam gives you a pearl.

89
00:03:44,014 --> 00:03:45,904
A new one grows in time.

90
00:03:48,009 --> 00:03:50,409
A sea urchin hurts when you touch it,

91
00:03:50,409 --> 00:03:51,979
and drops spines.

92
00:03:52,389 --> 00:03:54,189
A wild pineapple bush is ripe

93
00:03:54,189 --> 00:03:56,299
when its fruit turns golden.

94
00:03:56,589 --> 00:03:58,449
And a bubble vent makes a bubble column,

95
00:03:58,449 --> 00:04:01,199
where divers can catch their breath.

96
00:04:04,159 --> 00:04:05,819
The sea is full of places

97
00:04:05,819 --> 00:04:08,599
to explore: seven places of the story,

98
00:04:08,599 --> 00:04:10,649
and twelve smaller ones.

99
00:04:11,039 --> 00:04:12,949
Almost all of them have chests,

100
00:04:13,179 --> 00:04:14,849
each with its own loot.

101
00:04:17,334 --> 00:04:18,974
The old lighthouse stands

102
00:04:18,974 --> 00:04:20,524
on a rocky base.

103
00:04:20,914 --> 00:04:22,434
A spiral stair leads up

104
00:04:22,434 --> 00:04:24,944
to the lantern room with its great lens,

105
00:04:25,234 --> 00:04:27,114
and next to it are the keeper's cottage

106
00:04:27,114 --> 00:04:29,624
and a small dock with buoys.

107
00:04:32,334 --> 00:04:34,914
Saltmere is an abandoned fishing village

108
00:04:34,914 --> 00:04:36,784
on stilts above the reef,

109
00:04:37,154 --> 00:04:39,014
with huts, rope bridges,

110
00:04:39,014 --> 00:04:40,884
a little market and a shrine.

111
00:04:43,784 --> 00:04:45,704
Helix Research Station rests

112
00:04:45,704 --> 00:04:48,344
on the sea floor: glass domes

113
00:04:48,344 --> 00:04:50,274
and tunnels, an airlock,

114
00:04:50,504 --> 00:04:53,264
labs with research terminals, aquariums,

115
00:04:53,264 --> 00:04:54,654
and a flooded wing.

116
00:04:57,409 --> 00:05:00,119
Port Solace is the drowned city.

117
00:05:00,509 --> 00:05:02,799
Asphalt streets with wrecked cars,

118
00:05:03,029 --> 00:05:06,289
a plaza with a statue, and skyscrapers,

119
00:05:06,289 --> 00:05:08,389
some so tall that their broken tops

120
00:05:08,389 --> 00:05:10,019
reach above the waves.

121
00:05:10,469 --> 00:05:11,209
In the middle stands

122
00:05:11,209 --> 00:05:13,199
the City Hall tower.

123
00:05:14,984 --> 00:05:17,104
The Ashen Forge is a temple

124
00:05:17,104 --> 00:05:18,964
of the Tidewardens,

125
00:05:18,964 --> 00:05:20,994
built into the slope of a volcano,

126
00:05:21,684 --> 00:05:24,694
with channels of lava, a giant forge,

127
00:05:24,964 --> 00:05:25,884
and a vault behind

128
00:05:25,884 --> 00:05:27,854
a bridge over the fire.

129
00:05:29,560 --> 00:05:32,280
The Coral Temple rises from the reef,

130
00:05:32,280 --> 00:05:34,009
overgrown and half flooded,

131
00:05:34,220 --> 00:05:36,360
with a courtyard, colonnades,

132
00:05:36,360 --> 00:05:38,710
statues and an inner sanctum.

133
00:05:41,235 --> 00:05:41,975
And deep

134
00:05:41,975 --> 00:05:44,725
in the trench waits the Abyssal Sanctum.

135
00:05:44,915 --> 00:05:46,935
Its walls cannot be broken,

136
00:05:46,935 --> 00:05:49,564
and only one key opens its seal.

137
00:05:51,460 --> 00:05:53,420
A pirate galleon lies tilted

138
00:05:53,420 --> 00:05:54,220
on the floor,

139
00:05:54,220 --> 00:05:56,940
with broken masts, cannons,

140
00:05:56,940 --> 00:05:59,390
a captain's cabin and a cargo hold.

141
00:06:00,060 --> 00:06:02,140
Its chests hold gold coins,

142
00:06:02,140 --> 00:06:03,970
cannonballs and cutlasses,

143
00:06:04,140 --> 00:06:06,250
and sometimes a treasure chart.

144
00:06:09,160 --> 00:06:11,600
A rusty cargo ship broke in two,

145
00:06:11,600 --> 00:06:13,120
and spilled its shipping

146
00:06:13,120 --> 00:06:15,390
containers across the floor.

147
00:06:18,185 --> 00:06:19,785
Small fishing boats sank

148
00:06:19,785 --> 00:06:21,495
with their nets and crates.

149
00:06:24,410 --> 00:06:26,490
The pirate Saltjaw hid his cove

150
00:06:26,490 --> 00:06:29,550
inside a rocky island: a sea entrance,

151
00:06:29,550 --> 00:06:31,170
a dock with a ship,

152
00:06:31,170 --> 00:06:33,720
and a treasure room full of gold.

153
00:06:36,760 --> 00:06:38,220
The rusted rig stands

154
00:06:38,220 --> 00:06:41,190
on steel legs high above the open sea,

155
00:06:41,460 --> 00:06:44,620
with cranes, containers, a helipad,

156
00:06:44,620 --> 00:06:47,070
a radio mast and a wind turbine.

157
00:06:50,185 --> 00:06:53,085
Crashed planes rest on the sea floor,

158
00:06:53,085 --> 00:06:55,925
an airliner and a seaplane.

159
00:06:57,985 --> 00:07:00,525
Small Tidewarden ruins lie scattered

160
00:07:00,525 --> 00:07:02,805
on the reefs: columns,

161
00:07:02,805 --> 00:07:04,855
arches and broken statues.

162
00:07:08,010 --> 00:07:09,610
On palm isles you

163
00:07:09,610 --> 00:07:11,720
find tiny castaway camps,

164
00:07:12,050 --> 00:07:12,940
with a shelter,

165
00:07:13,250 --> 00:07:16,100
a campfire and an SOS in the sand.

166
00:07:19,060 --> 00:07:21,660
Abandoned rafts drift on the open sea,

167
00:07:21,660 --> 00:07:23,400
with a sail,

168
00:07:23,400 --> 00:07:25,230
a chest and a little farm.

169
00:07:28,160 --> 00:07:29,400
In the frost floes,

170
00:07:29,400 --> 00:07:30,880
a research hut sits

171
00:07:30,880 --> 00:07:33,570
on the ice: the iceberg outpost.

172
00:07:36,710 --> 00:07:38,410
Beach shacks are little bars,

173
00:07:38,410 --> 00:07:40,330
with deck chairs,

174
00:07:40,330 --> 00:07:42,180
umbrellas and tiki torches.

175
00:07:45,210 --> 00:07:47,390
And a buoy field marks a channel,

176
00:07:47,390 --> 00:07:48,890
with a supply crate

177
00:07:48,890 --> 00:07:50,760
chained between the buoys.

178
00:07:54,735 --> 00:07:56,375
The sea is full of life.

179
00:07:56,375 --> 00:07:58,295
Most creatures are peaceful.

180
00:07:58,295 --> 00:08:00,505
A few of them bite back.

181
00:08:01,935 --> 00:08:05,445
Bruce the shark hunts anyone who swims.

182
00:08:05,595 --> 00:08:07,195
On your raft you are safe,

183
00:08:07,195 --> 00:08:09,795
but your raft is not: he circles it

184
00:08:09,795 --> 00:08:11,155
and bites the edge foundations,

185
00:08:11,155 --> 00:08:13,145
until one breaks.

186
00:08:13,595 --> 00:08:16,425
Reinforced foundations are never bitten.

187
00:08:18,360 --> 00:08:20,500
The hammerhead is bigger and tougher,

188
00:08:20,500 --> 00:08:23,390
and lives in the deep, open sea.

189
00:08:25,110 --> 00:08:27,520
The whale is a gentle giant.

190
00:08:27,970 --> 00:08:28,810
It cruises a few

191
00:08:28,810 --> 00:08:30,730
blocks below the surface,

192
00:08:30,730 --> 00:08:32,410
comes up to breathe and spout,

193
00:08:32,410 --> 00:08:34,460
and sings now and then.

194
00:08:36,560 --> 00:08:39,160
Manta rays glide through the warm shallows

195
00:08:39,160 --> 00:08:41,250
in slow, wide loops.

196
00:08:43,160 --> 00:08:45,510
Jellyfish drift and pulse.

197
00:08:46,120 --> 00:08:47,590
Moon jellies are white,

198
00:08:47,840 --> 00:08:49,040
crimson jellies red,

199
00:08:49,040 --> 00:08:50,220
and glow jellies light

200
00:08:50,220 --> 00:08:52,240
up the dark lagoons.

201
00:08:52,240 --> 00:08:53,260
Their touch stings,

202
00:08:53,260 --> 00:08:55,310
unless you wear a wetsuit.

203
00:08:57,110 --> 00:08:59,160
In the darkness of the trench,

204
00:08:59,490 --> 00:09:00,390
the anglerfish waits

205
00:09:00,390 --> 00:09:02,220
with its glowing lure,

206
00:09:02,370 --> 00:09:04,120
then darts forward to bite.

207
00:09:06,060 --> 00:09:08,040
Moray eels hide in holes

208
00:09:08,040 --> 00:09:09,750
in the reefs and ruins,

209
00:09:10,200 --> 00:09:11,360
with only their head showing,

210
00:09:11,360 --> 00:09:15,070
and lunge at anyone who swims too close.

211
00:09:16,960 --> 00:09:20,090
On the beaches, crabs scuttle sideways.

212
00:09:20,740 --> 00:09:21,540
Sprint towards one,

213
00:09:21,540 --> 00:09:24,030
and it digs itself into the sand.

214
00:09:25,960 --> 00:09:29,290
Ember crabs live on the volcanic isles.

215
00:09:29,540 --> 00:09:30,400
Up close they attack,

216
00:09:30,400 --> 00:09:32,450
and set you on fire.

217
00:09:34,309 --> 00:09:35,489
Seagulls fly

218
00:09:35,489 --> 00:09:38,509
in flocks over islands and rafts.

219
00:09:38,509 --> 00:09:39,209
They peck at crops

220
00:09:39,209 --> 00:09:41,049
and snatch food from the ground,

221
00:09:41,049 --> 00:09:43,919
unless a scarecrow stands nearby.

222
00:09:46,059 --> 00:09:48,419
Penguins waddle over the frost floes,

223
00:09:48,419 --> 00:09:50,279
slide on their bellies

224
00:09:50,279 --> 00:09:52,009
and dive for fish.

225
00:09:53,759 --> 00:09:55,799
Sea otters float on their backs

226
00:09:55,799 --> 00:09:56,859
in the kelp forest

227
00:09:56,859 --> 00:09:59,509
and crack shells on their bellies.

228
00:10:00,039 --> 00:10:02,739
Feed one a seashell, and it follows you,

229
00:10:02,739 --> 00:10:04,709
and brings you pearls.

230
00:10:06,609 --> 00:10:09,289
And the drowned corsairs are the cursed crew

231
00:10:09,289 --> 00:10:11,309
of the pirate Saltjaw.

232
00:10:11,309 --> 00:10:13,969
They swim, fight with cutlasses,

233
00:10:13,969 --> 00:10:16,379
and even climb onto rafts.

234
00:10:19,084 --> 00:10:21,944
Beach Craft adds more than three hundred blocks

235
00:10:21,944 --> 00:10:23,984
and items. They are sorted

236
00:10:23,984 --> 00:10:26,354
into six new creative tabs,

237
00:10:26,604 --> 00:10:29,874
plus the tab of Beach Craft two.

238
00:10:30,534 --> 00:10:32,674
Building: weathered and teak wood,

239
00:10:32,674 --> 00:10:35,834
sea glass, coral stone and tidestone,

240
00:10:35,834 --> 00:10:37,744
cracked concrete and asphalt,

241
00:10:38,374 --> 00:10:40,574
steel hulls, beams, catwalks,

242
00:10:40,574 --> 00:10:42,604
shipping containers and portholes.

243
00:10:57,559 --> 00:11:00,079
Decoration: paper lanterns

244
00:11:00,079 --> 00:11:01,259
in nine colours,

245
00:11:01,259 --> 00:11:03,999
string lights, buoys and neon tubes,

246
00:11:03,999 --> 00:11:05,379
furniture, treasure chests

247
00:11:05,379 --> 00:11:07,629
and everything a pirate needs.

248
00:11:18,659 --> 00:11:20,599
Nature: the sands,

249
00:11:20,599 --> 00:11:22,399
plants and sea life of the biomes,

250
00:11:22,399 --> 00:11:24,709
and the things they give you.

251
00:11:27,959 --> 00:11:30,069
Voyage: the boats,

252
00:11:30,279 --> 00:11:32,019
the expedition raft with its upgrades,

253
00:11:32,019 --> 00:11:33,769
and the diving gear.

254
00:11:36,184 --> 00:11:38,504
Creatures: the spawn eggs,

255
00:11:38,504 --> 00:11:40,114
and what the creatures drop.

256
00:11:46,484 --> 00:11:49,764
Tides of the Deep: the story items,

257
00:11:49,764 --> 00:11:50,884
the four sigils,

258
00:11:50,884 --> 00:11:52,464
the blocks of the sanctum,

259
00:11:52,464 --> 00:11:54,214
and the treasures of the Leviathan.

260
00:11:56,559 --> 00:11:57,779
And the Raft tab

261
00:11:57,779 --> 00:12:00,119
of Beach Craft two: driftwood

262
00:12:00,119 --> 00:12:01,439
and palm wood,

263
00:12:01,439 --> 00:12:04,259
raft foundations, the survival tools,

264
00:12:04,259 --> 00:12:05,889
titanium and the machines.

265
00:12:17,109 --> 00:12:19,109
The expedition raft is made

266
00:12:19,109 --> 00:12:20,659
from six foundations,

267
00:12:21,089 --> 00:12:22,759
two rope and a paddle.

268
00:12:23,089 --> 00:12:24,889
It is a big three by three raft,

269
00:12:24,889 --> 00:12:26,269
with four seats

270
00:12:26,269 --> 00:12:28,519
and twenty seven storage slots.

271
00:12:28,909 --> 00:12:31,309
It never sinks, it never tips over,

272
00:12:31,309 --> 00:12:33,279
and sharks cannot hurt it.

273
00:12:34,859 --> 00:12:36,939
Upgrades go right onto the raft,

274
00:12:36,939 --> 00:12:38,949
and every one of them shows.

275
00:12:39,599 --> 00:12:41,269
The sail makes it faster,

276
00:12:41,459 --> 00:12:43,769
the engine more than twice as fast,

277
00:12:44,019 --> 00:12:46,189
the cargo crate adds storage,

278
00:12:46,579 --> 00:12:47,899
lanterns light it up,

279
00:12:47,899 --> 00:12:49,849
and the anchor holds it in place.

280
00:12:51,884 --> 00:12:54,184
The palm boat and the driftwood raft

281
00:12:54,184 --> 00:12:55,664
work like vanilla boats,

282
00:12:55,664 --> 00:12:57,244
with or without a chest,

283
00:12:57,244 --> 00:12:58,504
and in a boat,

284
00:12:58,504 --> 00:13:00,734
the paddle gives you a push.

285
00:13:02,534 --> 00:13:04,984
For the deep there is diving gear.

286
00:13:05,334 --> 00:13:06,394
The diving helmet lets

287
00:13:06,394 --> 00:13:07,574
you see far under water,

288
00:13:07,574 --> 00:13:10,194
and with an oxygen tank you breathe

289
00:13:10,194 --> 00:13:11,404
from the tank.

290
00:13:11,734 --> 00:13:14,444
A gauge shows how much air is left.

291
00:13:16,184 --> 00:13:18,594
Crafted with an angler lure,

292
00:13:18,764 --> 00:13:19,924
the helmet gets a lamp,

293
00:13:19,924 --> 00:13:22,674
and the dark trench becomes visible.

294
00:13:24,434 --> 00:13:26,954
The wetsuit lets you mine faster under water

295
00:13:26,954 --> 00:13:29,064
and keeps jellyfish away,

296
00:13:29,314 --> 00:13:31,484
flippers make you swim much faster,

297
00:13:31,734 --> 00:13:32,474
and the full set

298
00:13:32,474 --> 00:13:34,304
gives you dolphin's grace.

299
00:13:36,109 --> 00:13:38,169
The air compressor refills tanks,

300
00:13:38,169 --> 00:13:41,259
with energy or with its hand crank.

301
00:13:42,784 --> 00:13:45,574
The harpoon gun shoots harpoons,

302
00:13:45,904 --> 00:13:47,804
eight damage under water,

303
00:13:47,804 --> 00:13:48,584
and the sea scooter

304
00:13:48,584 --> 00:13:50,254
pulls you through the deep.

305
00:13:52,184 --> 00:13:53,704
The ship cannon fires

306
00:13:53,704 --> 00:13:56,104
cannonballs about forty blocks far,

307
00:13:56,104 --> 00:13:58,374
without breaking any blocks.

308
00:14:00,784 --> 00:14:02,544
The wind turbine makes

309
00:14:02,544 --> 00:14:04,124
energy high above the sea,

310
00:14:04,124 --> 00:14:06,104
just like the solar panel.

311
00:14:06,104 --> 00:14:07,704
Cables carry it

312
00:14:07,704 --> 00:14:09,354
to batteries and machines.

313
00:14:11,384 --> 00:14:12,444
Chairs,

314
00:14:12,444 --> 00:14:14,964
cushions and deck chairs can be sat on,

315
00:14:14,964 --> 00:14:16,064
and the hammock is a real

316
00:14:16,064 --> 00:14:18,934
bed: it sets your spawn point.

317
00:14:20,609 --> 00:14:22,169
And when it gets dark,

318
00:14:22,169 --> 00:14:23,599
the lights come alive.

319
00:14:26,159 --> 00:14:26,919
The tools

320
00:14:26,919 --> 00:14:29,549
of raft survival are still here.

321
00:14:29,839 --> 00:14:31,779
The item catcher fishes debris out

322
00:14:31,779 --> 00:14:32,919
of the water,

323
00:14:32,919 --> 00:14:35,219
the water purifier turns sea water

324
00:14:35,219 --> 00:14:37,699
into fresh water, and the simple grill

325
00:14:37,699 --> 00:14:39,969
cooks two foods at once.

326
00:14:41,559 --> 00:14:43,909
Crop plots never dry out,

327
00:14:44,159 --> 00:14:46,359
pineapples grow from their crowns,

328
00:14:46,359 --> 00:14:48,949
and a scarecrow keeps the seagulls away.

329
00:14:50,409 --> 00:14:53,309
The machines of Beach Craft two still run

330
00:14:53,309 --> 00:14:55,639
on energy: the quarry,

331
00:14:55,849 --> 00:14:57,109
the chunk destroyer,

332
00:14:57,109 --> 00:14:59,359
and the brick and titanium furnaces.

333
00:15:01,109 --> 00:15:02,189
The Seafarer's

334
00:15:02,189 --> 00:15:04,639
Almanac explains everything,

335
00:15:04,909 --> 00:15:06,349
chapter by chapter,

336
00:15:06,349 --> 00:15:08,799
with a page for every creature.

337
00:15:10,584 --> 00:15:13,244
Research terminals still show the logs

338
00:15:13,244 --> 00:15:14,634
of the expedition,

339
00:15:15,024 --> 00:15:16,544
and old radios crackle

340
00:15:16,544 --> 00:15:18,914
with broadcasts from long ago.

341
00:15:21,809 --> 00:15:23,649
Now let us follow the story,

342
00:15:23,649 --> 00:15:24,989
the way a player would.

343
00:15:24,989 --> 00:15:27,519
From here on, there are spoilers.

344
00:15:29,409 --> 00:15:33,709
On the arrival platform waits a castaway chest: a note

345
00:15:33,709 --> 00:15:35,529
from Captain Rhea Marlow,

346
00:15:35,529 --> 00:15:37,859
the expedition journal, a chart,

347
00:15:38,069 --> 00:15:39,939
and a basic kit to survive.

348
00:15:43,084 --> 00:15:45,164
The expedition journal always

349
00:15:45,164 --> 00:15:46,854
knows the next goal.

350
00:15:47,104 --> 00:15:49,154
The first one is the Old Lighthouse.

351
00:15:51,134 --> 00:15:52,894
With a raft and the chart,

352
00:15:52,894 --> 00:15:53,944
you set sail.

353
00:15:56,109 --> 00:15:58,949
In the keeper's cottage lies the logbook

354
00:15:58,949 --> 00:16:01,209
of Tobias Fenn, and a chart

355
00:16:01,209 --> 00:16:03,539
to the stilt village of Saltmere.

356
00:16:06,434 --> 00:16:08,954
In Saltmere, the elder's hut holds

357
00:16:08,954 --> 00:16:10,964
Nana Kalea's letters,

358
00:16:11,234 --> 00:16:13,444
a diving helmet and the next chart.

359
00:16:13,874 --> 00:16:14,774
And behind the statue

360
00:16:14,774 --> 00:16:16,234
in the shrine lies the

361
00:16:16,234 --> 00:16:18,784
first sigil: the Coral Sigil.

362
00:16:21,659 --> 00:16:24,569
Deep below, at Helix Station,

363
00:16:24,799 --> 00:16:26,399
the terminals of Dr.

364
00:16:26,399 --> 00:16:28,879
Imara Voss tell how the expedition drilled

365
00:16:28,879 --> 00:16:31,609
into the abyss, and woke something.

366
00:16:32,099 --> 00:16:34,729
Her lab vault holds the Pearl Sigil.

367
00:16:37,434 --> 00:16:39,294
In Port Solace,

368
00:16:39,294 --> 00:16:41,414
Mayor Crane sealed the Storm Sigil

369
00:16:41,414 --> 00:16:42,754
in a vault near the top

370
00:16:42,754 --> 00:16:44,504
of the City Hall tower.

371
00:16:47,334 --> 00:16:49,204
In the Ashen Forge,

372
00:16:49,434 --> 00:16:51,434
the Ember Sigil waits beyond the river

373
00:16:51,434 --> 00:16:52,584
of fire.

374
00:16:55,509 --> 00:16:57,709
With all four sigils,

375
00:16:57,709 --> 00:16:59,069
the altar of the Coral Temple

376
00:16:59,069 --> 00:17:01,439
forges the Tidewarden Key.

377
00:17:03,584 --> 00:17:05,564
The key opens the Tide Seal

378
00:17:05,564 --> 00:17:07,484
of the Abyssal Sanctum.

379
00:17:07,484 --> 00:17:09,724
Behind it lies a dome full of air,

380
00:17:09,724 --> 00:17:11,754
around a deep pool.

381
00:17:13,709 --> 00:17:14,649
At the altar

382
00:17:14,649 --> 00:17:16,569
on the edge of the pool,

383
00:17:16,569 --> 00:17:18,219
the key wakes the Leviathan,

384
00:17:18,629 --> 00:17:20,009
a colossal sea serpent

385
00:17:20,009 --> 00:17:21,959
with six hundred health.

386
00:17:24,284 --> 00:17:25,704
It circles in the pool,

387
00:17:25,704 --> 00:17:27,584
where nothing can hurt it.

388
00:17:27,584 --> 00:17:30,174
It rises, and spits brine bolts.

389
00:17:32,134 --> 00:17:34,694
It leaps across the stone ring,

390
00:17:34,694 --> 00:17:35,434
slams down,

391
00:17:35,434 --> 00:17:38,144
and lies stranded for four seconds.

392
00:17:38,594 --> 00:17:40,284
That is the moment to strike.

393
00:17:42,209 --> 00:17:43,829
Below half health,

394
00:17:43,829 --> 00:17:45,729
it roars and calls the tidelings,

395
00:17:45,729 --> 00:17:47,589
and stirs a whirlpool

396
00:17:47,589 --> 00:17:49,799
that pulls you towards the pool.

397
00:17:50,389 --> 00:17:53,059
Below a quarter, it gets faster still.

398
00:17:55,159 --> 00:17:56,459
When it falls,

399
00:17:56,459 --> 00:17:58,229
it leaves the Heart of the Tide,

400
00:17:58,479 --> 00:18:00,829
leviathan scales, and its trophy.

401
00:18:03,309 --> 00:18:04,949
Placed in the water,

402
00:18:04,949 --> 00:18:06,409
the Heart of the Tide gives every

403
00:18:06,409 --> 00:18:08,429
swimmer nearby conduit power

404
00:18:08,429 --> 00:18:11,559
and dolphin's grace. Four scales,

405
00:18:12,169 --> 00:18:13,229
titanium and a trident

406
00:18:13,229 --> 00:18:15,624
make the Tidebreaker.

407
00:18:16,484 --> 00:18:19,234
And the journal has one last entry.

408
00:18:19,404 --> 00:18:20,574
The sea is calm.

409
00:18:20,884 --> 00:18:22,834
Thank you, keeper of the tides.

410
00:18:25,309 --> 00:18:28,199
This was Beach Craft three point oh.

411
00:18:28,529 --> 00:18:29,909
Free on CurseForge,

412
00:18:29,909 --> 00:18:31,519
the link is in the description.

